    10	\chapter{Physics problem IPhO\_2026\_3\_A\_3}
    11	\label{ch:IPhO2026Problems_problem_IPhO_2026_3_A_3}
    12	
    13	\paragraph{Problem source.}
    14	A homogeneous isotropic paramagnetic torus has mean radius R, inner radius r
    15	with r << R, volume V, and cross-sectional area A.  An insulated conducting
    16	wire is wound densely around it with N turns and instantaneous current I.
    17	Fields H and B and magnetization M are approximately uniform in the torus.
    18	Use B = mu\_0*H + mu\_0*M, Ampere's law, and the sign convention that work and
    19	heat entering the paramagnetic torus are positive.
    20	
    21	Current subquestion:
    22	Subtract the vacuum-core contribution and write the work dW done on the paramagnetic material.
    23	
    24	\paragraph{Current subquestion.}
    25	Subtract the vacuum-core contribution and write the work dW done on the paramagnetic material.
    26	
    27	\paragraph{Recorded answer/context.}
    28	dW = mu\_0*V*H*dM.
    29	
    30	\paragraph{Figure/image path.}
    31	/root/proposal\_for\_physic/science-mango/ipho\_2026\_source/image/T3\_page-2.png
    32	
    33	\paragraph{Reusable previous-part conclusions.}
    34	\begin{itemize}
    35	\item Source A.2. Question: Find the work dW\_emf performed by the external voltage source when B changes by dB. Reusable conclusions: dW\_emf = V*H*dB. Policy: natural\_language\_prerequisite\_only; do\_not\_import\_Lean\_output
    36	\end{itemize}
    37	
    38	\paragraph{Formalization target.}
    39	create a compiling Lean file with sorry bodies at `IPhO2026Problems/problem\_IPhO\_2026\_3\_A\_3.lean`.
    40	The Lean declarations must preserve the physical quantities, dimensions or dimensional roles, figure labels, governing-law hypotheses, and final relation expressed by this problem.
    41	Use Mathlib/Physlib names found through LeanExplore where available. If a domain API is missing, introduce faithful local abstractions rather than scalar placeholder aliases.
